       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any clinical indication that supports it. For a 70 kg adult with normal organ function, the risk of serious harm is high. That includes serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and death. I can't enter it as written.\n\nI can do any of these instead:\n- Enter sertraline at a standard dose (50 mg, 100 mg, or up to 200 mg once daily), with a note if you want one.\n- Enter a titration schedule, such as stepping up 50 mg at a time at appropriate intervals toward 200 mg.\n- Help you prepare a note for a pharmacy or psychiatry consult if you think this patient needs something unusual.\n\nIf you think I've misunderstood the situation, for example if the dose is meant to be something else or the order comes from a protocol I don't know about, tell me and I'll reconsider. If you need to enter the order as written, you'd have to do it directly in the order-entry system, where pharmacy verification and the system's dose-range checks will apply."
